IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 25C and 25D.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively): constitutional limitations on transactions with directors or their associates (s 25C), and who is a person connected with a director (s 25D).
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 25C(1) and (2): when the section applies, and what it leaves alone`

-- "This section applies to a transaction if or to the extent that its validity depends on section 25B." An "if" gate on applicability (reading (a) for a lawyer: a failed "if" is the text's no; fork line F-I4).
-- src:4351 | 25C.—(1) This section applies to a transaction if or to the extent
-- src:4352 | that its validity depends on section 25B.
@ref s 25C(1) (src:4351-4352)
GIVEN `the validity of the transaction depends on section 25B, wholly or to some extent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(1) section 25C applies to the transaction` MEANS
    IF `the validity of the transaction depends on section 25B, wholly or to some extent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a transaction if or to the extent that its validity depends on section 25B." (a condition the text introduces with "if")

-- "Nothing in this section is to be construed as excluding the operation of any other written law or rule of law by virtue of which the transaction may be called in question or any liability to the company may arise."
-- src:4356 | (2) Nothing in this section is to be construed as excluding the
-- src:4357 | operation of any other written law or rule of law by virtue of which
-- src:4358 | the transaction may be called in question or any liability to the
-- src:4359 | company may arise.
@ref s 25C(2) (src:4356-4359)
GIVEN `the other written law or rule of law is one by virtue of which the transaction may be called in question or a liability to the company may arise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(2) section 25C excludes the operation of the other written law or rule of law` MEANS
    IF `the other written law or rule of law is one by virtue of which the transaction may be called in question or a liability to the company may arise`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section is to be construed as excluding the operation of any other written law or rule of law by virtue of which the transaction may be called in question or any liability to the company may arise."
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving is of a law by virtue of which the transaction may be called in question or a liability to the company may arise

§ `Section 25C(3): the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company`

-- "Where (a) a company enters into such a transaction; and (b) the parties to the transaction include (i) a director of the company or of its holding company; or (ii) a person connected with any such director,
-- the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company." A "where" gate: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), gives JUST FALSE when it fails (fork line F-I5). "Voidable" is a status, not "may".
-- src:4363 | (3) Where —
-- src:4365 | (a) a company enters into such a transaction; and
-- src:4367 | (b) the parties to the transaction include —
-- src:4369 | (i) a director of the company or of its holding company;
-- src:4370 | or
-- src:4372 | (ii) a person connected with any such director,
-- src:4374 | the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company.
@ref s 25C(3) (src:4363-4374)
GIVEN `the company has entered into a transaction to which section 25C applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties to the transaction include a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties to the transaction include a person connected with such a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(3) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` MEANS
    IF    `the company has entered into a transaction to which section 25C applies`
      AND (   `the parties to the transaction include a director of the company or of its holding company`
           OR `the parties to the transaction include a person connected with such a director`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where — (a) a company enters into such a transaction; and (b) the parties to the transaction include — (i) a director of the company or of its holding company; or (ii) a person connected with any such director, the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company." (a "where" condition: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-I5)

§ `Section 25C(4), (5) and (6): liability, when the transaction ceases to be voidable`

-- (4): "Whether or not it is avoided, any such party to the transaction as is mentioned in subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director of the company who authorised the transaction, is liable".
-- src:4378 | (4) Whether or not it is avoided, any such party to the transaction as
-- src:4379 | is mentioned in subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director of the
-- src:4380 | company who authorised the transaction, is liable —
-- src:4382 | (a) to account to the company for any gain the party or the
-- src:4383 | director has made directly or indirectly by the transaction;
-- src:4384 | and
-- src:4386 | (b) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting
-- src:4387 | from the transaction.
@ref s 25C(4) (src:4378-4387)
GIVEN `the person is a party to the transaction who is a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with such a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company who authorised the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(4) the person is liable to the company under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a party to the transaction who is a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with such a director`
       OR `the person is a director of the company who authorised the transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such party ... and any director of the company who authorised the transaction, is liable" names two classes and says nothing of anyone else (the list is not closed with "only")

-- (6): "A person other than a director of the company is not liable under subsection (4) if the person shows that at the time the transaction was entered into the person did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers."
-- src:4411 | (6) A person other than a director of the company is not liable under
-- src:4412 | subsection (4) if the person shows that at the time the transaction was
-- src:4413 | entered into the person did not know that the directors were exceeding
-- src:4414 | their powers.
@ref s 25C(6) (src:4411-4414)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that at the time the transaction was entered into the person did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(6) the person other than a director is liable under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the person is a director of the company`)
      AND `the person shows that at the time the transaction was entered into the person did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person other than a director of the company is not liable under subsection (4) if the person shows that at the time the transaction was entered into the person did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers." (a flat negative with an "if")
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): for a director, and for a person who does not show that, subsection (6) says nothing; subsection (4) answers

-- Subsections (4) and (6) together: liable under (4) unless (6) says the person is not.
-- src:4378 | (4) Whether or not it is avoided, any such party to the transaction as
-- src:4379 | is mentioned in subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director of the
-- src:4380 | company who authorised the transaction, is liable —
-- src:4382 | (a) to account to the company for any gain the party or the
-- src:4383 | director has made directly or indirectly by the transaction;
-- src:4384 | and
-- src:4386 | (b) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting
-- src:4387 | from the transaction.
@ref s 25C(4) (src:4378-4387)
GIVEN `the person is a party to the transaction who is a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with such a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company who authorised the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that at the time the transaction was entered into the person did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(4) and (6) the person is liable to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 25C(6) the person other than a director is liable under subsection (4)` `the person is a director of the company` `the person shows that at the time the transaction was entered into the person did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (6) takes the person out of subsection (4)
    ELSE `s 25C(4) the person is liable to the company under subsection (4)` `the person is a party to the transaction who is a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with such a director` `the person is a director of the company who authorised the transaction`

-- (4)(a): "to account to the company for any gain the party or the director has made directly or indirectly by the transaction". A sum: the gain.
-- src:4378 | (4) Whether or not it is avoided, any such party to the transaction as
-- src:4379 | is mentioned in subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director of the
-- src:4380 | company who authorised the transaction, is liable —
-- src:4382 | (a) to account to the company for any gain the party or the
-- src:4383 | director has made directly or indirectly by the transaction;
-- src:4384 | and
@ref s 25C(4)(a) (src:4378-4384)
GIVEN `the person is liable to the company under subsection (4) and not excused by subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gain the person has made, directly or indirectly, by the transaction, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 25C(4)(a) the amount the person must account to the company for` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable to the company under subsection (4) and not excused by subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST `the gain the person has made, directly or indirectly, by the transaction, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph states a sum only for a person who is liable under subsection (4)

-- (4)(b): "to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction". A sum: the loss or damage.
-- src:4378 | (4) Whether or not it is avoided, any such party to the transaction as
-- src:4379 | is mentioned in subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director of the
-- src:4380 | company who authorised the transaction, is liable —
-- src:4382 | (a) to account to the company for any gain the party or the
-- src:4383 | director has made directly or indirectly by the transaction;
-- src:4384 | and
-- src:4386 | (b) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting
-- src:4387 | from the transaction.
@ref s 25C(4)(b) (src:4378-4387)
GIVEN `the person is liable to the company under subsection (4) and not excused by subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(4)(b) the person must indemnify the company for the loss or damage` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable to the company under subsection (4) and not excused by subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph states the duty only for a person who is liable under subsection (4)

GIVEN `the person is liable to the company under subsection (4) and not excused by subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss or damage to the company resulting from the transaction, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 25C(4)(b) the amount the person must indemnify the company for` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable to the company under subsection (4) and not excused by subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST `the loss or damage to the company resulting from the transaction, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph states a sum only for a person who is liable under subsection (4)

-- (5): "The transaction ceases to be voidable if (a) restitution ... is no longer possible; (b) the company is indemnified ...; (c) rights acquired bona fide for value and without actual notice ... would be affected by the avoidance; or (d) the transaction is affirmed by the company."
-- An "if" the text introduces: a failed "if" is the text's no (reading (a) for a lawyer; fork line F-I4).
-- src:4394 | (5) The transaction ceases to be voidable if —
-- src:4396 | (a) restitution of any money or other asset which was the
-- src:4397 | subject matter of the transaction is no longer possible;
-- src:4399 | (b) the company is indemnified for any loss or damage
-- src:4400 | resulting from the transaction;
-- src:4402 | (c) rights acquired bona fide for value and without actual
-- src:4403 | notice of the directors exceeding their powers by a person
-- src:4404 | who is not party to the transaction would be affected by the
-- src:4405 | avoidance; or
-- src:4407 | (d) the transaction is affirmed by the company.
@ref s 25C(5) (src:4394-4407)
GIVEN `restitution of any money or other asset which was the subject matter of the transaction is no longer possible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rights acquired bona fide for value and without actual notice of the directors exceeding their powers by a person who is not party to the transaction would be affected by the avoidance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is affirmed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(5) the transaction ceases to be voidable` MEANS
    IF    `restitution of any money or other asset which was the subject matter of the transaction is no longer possible`
       OR `the company is indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction`
       OR `rights acquired bona fide for value and without actual notice of the directors exceeding their powers by a person who is not party to the transaction would be affected by the avoidance`
       OR `the transaction is affirmed by the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The transaction ceases to be voidable if — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..." (a condition the text introduces with "if"; reading (a) for a lawyer, fork line F-I4)

§ `Section 25C(7) and (8): parties outside subsection (3)(b), the Court's order, and "transaction"`

-- (7), first limb: "Nothing in subsections (1) to (6) affects the rights of any party to the transaction not within subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii)".
-- src:4418 | (7) Nothing in subsections (1) to (6) affects the rights of any party
-- src:4419 | to the transaction not within subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii); but the court
-- src:4420 | may, on the application of the company or any such party, make an
-- src:4421 | order affirming, severing or setting aside the transaction on such
-- src:4422 | terms as appear to the court to be just.
@ref s 25C(7) (src:4418-4422)
GIVEN `the party is a party to the transaction who is neither a director of the company or of its holding company nor a person connected with such a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(7) subsections (1) to (6) affect the rights of the party` MEANS
    IF `the party is a party to the transaction who is neither a director of the company or of its holding company nor a person connected with such a director`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsections (1) to (6) affects the rights of any party to the transaction not within subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii)"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving is of a party "not within subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii)"; for a party within it, subsections (1) to (6) answer

-- (7), second limb: "the court may, on the application of the company or any such party, make an order affirming, severing or setting aside the transaction on such terms as appear to the court to be just."
-- A "may" gated by "on the application of": split site (ii) (fork line F-I6); NOTHING where there is no such application (the grant ruling), the other reading being JUST FALSE (the periods ruling, item (b), with "upon" counting as "where").
-- src:4418 | (7) Nothing in subsections (1) to (6) affects the rights of any party
-- src:4419 | to the transaction not within subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii); but the court
-- src:4420 | may, on the application of the company or any such party, make an
-- src:4421 | order affirming, severing or setting aside the transaction on such
-- src:4422 | terms as appear to the court to be just.
@ref s 25C(7) (src:4418-4422)
GIVEN `the application is made by the company or by a party to the transaction not within subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(7) the court may make an order affirming, severing or setting aside the transaction` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by the company or by a party to the transaction not within subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, on the application of the company or any such party, make an order ..." -- a power gated by "on the application of"; where no such application is made the text names no outcome (split site (ii), fork line F-I6)

-- (8): "In this section, 'transaction' includes any act." "includes": the list is open.
-- src:4426 | (8) In this section, “transaction” includes any act.
@ref s 25C(8) (src:4426-4426)
GIVEN `the thing is an act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C(8) the thing is within the word transaction` MEANS
    IF `the thing is an act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "'transaction' includes any act" does not close the meaning

§ `Section 25C(4): the duties as regulative rules`

-- The text names the bearer of each duty in s 25C(4) (the party mentioned in (3)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director who authorised the transaction) and the act. Neither has a time limit or a stated consequence,
-- so no trace can show either breached (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sgi)").
DECLARE `s 25C(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 25C(4)(a) account to the company for any gain made directly or indirectly by the transaction`
    `s 25C(4)(b) indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction`

-- src:4378 | (4) Whether or not it is avoided, any such party to the transaction as
-- src:4379 | is mentioned in subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director of the
-- src:4380 | company who authorised the transaction, is liable —
-- src:4382 | (a) to account to the company for any gain the party or the
-- src:4383 | director has made directly or indirectly by the transaction;
-- src:4384 | and
@ref s 25C(4)(a) (src:4378-4384)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 25C(4) act`
`s 25C(4)(a) the person liable under subsection (4) must account to the company for any gain` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 25C(4)(a) account to the company for any gain made directly or indirectly by the transaction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 25C(4)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person did not account to the company for any gain made directly or indirectly by the transaction" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:4378 | (4) Whether or not it is avoided, any such party to the transaction as
-- src:4379 | is mentioned in subsection (3)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director of the
-- src:4380 | company who authorised the transaction, is liable —
-- src:4382 | (a) to account to the company for any gain the party or the
-- src:4383 | director has made directly or indirectly by the transaction;
-- src:4384 | and
-- src:4386 | (b) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting
-- src:4387 | from the transaction.
@ref s 25C(4)(b) (src:4378-4387)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 25C(4) act`
`s 25C(4)(b) the person liable under subsection (4) must indemnify the company for any loss or damage` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 25C(4)(b) indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 25C(4)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person did not indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

§ `Section 25D(2)(a) to (e): the meanings used by section 25D(1)`

DECLARE `s 25D(2)(a) relationship to the director` IS ONE OF
    `s 25D(2)(a) spouse`
    `s 25D(2)(a) son`
    `s 25D(2)(a) adopted son`
    `s 25D(2)(a) stepson`
    `s 25D(2)(a) daughter`
    `s 25D(2)(a) adopted daughter`
    `s 25D(2)(a) stepdaughter`
    `s 25D(2)(a) another relationship`

-- (a): "a member of a director's family includes the director's spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and stepdaughter". "includes": the list is open.
-- src:4485 | (a) a member of a director’s family includes the director’s
-- src:4486 | spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted
-- src:4487 | daughter and stepdaughter;
@ref s 25D(2)(a) (src:4485-4487)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 25D(2)(a) relationship to the director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25D(2)(a) the person is a member of the director's family` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 25D(2)(a) another relationship` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the director's spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and stepdaughter" does not close the list
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (b): "a director is connected with a body corporate if, and only if, the director and the persons connected with the director together (i) are interested in at least 20% of the share capital of that body corporate;
-- or (ii) are entitled to exercise or control, directly or indirectly, the exercise of more than 20% of the voting power at any general meeting of that body corporate". "if, and only if": closed.
-- The percentages are taken as plain numbers, as the caller adds up the interests (s 7 gives the meaning of an interest in shares: a caller that wants it uses sg-interests.l4).
-- src:4489 | (b) a director is connected with a body corporate if, and only if,
-- src:4490 | the director and the persons connected with the director
-- src:4491 | together —
-- src:4496 | (i) are interested in at least 20% of the share capital of
-- src:4497 | that body corporate; or
-- src:4499 | (ii) are entitled to exercise or control, directly or
-- src:4500 | indirectly, the exercise of more than 20% of the
-- src:4501 | voting power at any general meeting of that body
-- src:4502 | corporate;
@ref s 25D(2)(b) (src:4489-4502)
GIVEN `the percentage of the share capital of the body corporate in which the director and the persons connected with the director together are interested` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the voting power at any general meeting of the body corporate that the director and the persons connected with the director together are entitled to exercise or control, directly or indirectly` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25D(2)(b) the director is connected with the body corporate` MEANS
    IF    `the percentage of the share capital of the body corporate in which the director and the persons connected with the director together are interested` AT LEAST 20
       OR `the percentage of the voting power at any general meeting of the body corporate that the director and the persons connected with the director together are entitled to exercise or control, directly or indirectly` GREATER THAN 20
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a director is connected with a body corporate if, and only if, the director and the persons connected with the director together (i) are interested in at least 20% of the share capital of that body corporate; or (ii) are entitled to exercise or control, directly or indirectly, the exercise of more than 20% of the voting power at any general meeting of that body corporate" (a condition closed with "only if")

-- (c): "a reference in paragraph (b)(ii) to voting power the exercise of which is controlled by a director includes voting power whose exercise is controlled by a body corporate controlled by the director". "includes".
-- src:4504 | (c) a reference in paragraph (b)(ii) to voting power the
-- src:4505 | exercise of which is controlled by a director includes
-- src:4506 | voting power whose exercise is controlled by a body
-- src:4507 | corporate controlled by the director;
@ref s 25D(2)(c) (src:4504-4507)
GIVEN `the voting power is controlled by the director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voting power is controlled by a body corporate controlled by the director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25D(2)(c) the voting power counts as voting power the exercise of which is controlled by the director` MEANS
    IF    `the voting power is controlled by the director`
       OR `the voting power is controlled by a body corporate controlled by the director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes voting power whose exercise is controlled by a body corporate controlled by the director" does not close the meaning

-- (d)(i): "a body corporate with which a director is connected is not treated for the purposes of this subsection as connected with the director unless it is also connected with the director by virtue of subsection (1)(c) or (d)".
-- Once the "unless" is met the paragraph is silent (the answer then comes from s 25D(1)(c) or (d)): NOTHING (one of the six case-by-case questions of 2026-11-05; fork line F-I7).
-- src:4509 | (d) to avoid circularity in the application of subsection (1) —
-- src:4511 | (i) a body corporate with which a director is connected
-- src:4512 | is not treated for the purposes of this subsection as
-- src:4513 | connected with the director unless it is also
-- src:4514 | connected with the director by virtue of
-- src:4515 | subsection (1)(c) or (d); and
@ref s 25D(2)(d)(i) (src:4509-4515)
GIVEN `the director is connected with the body corporate by virtue of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is also connected with the director by virtue of subsection (1)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25D(2)(d)(i) the body corporate is treated as connected with the director for the purposes of subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the director is connected with the body corporate by virtue of paragraph (b)`
    THEN (IF `the body corporate is also connected with the director by virtue of subsection (1)(c) or (d)`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the "unless" is met, and the paragraph then says nothing of whether the body corporate is treated as connected (subsection (1)(c) or (d) answers; fork line F-I7)
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a body corporate with which a director is connected is not treated for the purposes of this subsection as connected with the director unless it is also connected with the director by virtue of subsection (1)(c) or (d)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "a body corporate with which a director is connected"

-- (d)(ii): "a trustee of a trust the beneficiaries of which include (or may include) a body corporate with which a director is connected is not treated for the purposes of this subsection as connected with a director by reason only of that fact".
-- src:4517 | (ii) a trustee of a trust the beneficiaries of which include
-- src:4518 | (or may include) a body corporate with which a
-- src:4519 | director is connected is not treated for the purposes
-- src:4520 | of this subsection as connected with a director by
-- src:4521 | reason only of that fact; and
@ref s 25D(2)(d)(ii) (src:4517-4521)
GIVEN `the trust's beneficiaries include, or may include, a body corporate with which the director is connected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that fact is the only reason for treating the trustee as connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25D(2)(d)(ii) the trustee is treated as connected with the director for the purposes of subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF    `the trust's beneficiaries include, or may include, a body corporate with which the director is connected`
      AND `that fact is the only reason for treating the trustee as connected with the director`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a trustee of a trust the beneficiaries of which include (or may include) a body corporate with which a director is connected is not treated for the purposes of this subsection as connected with a director by reason only of that fact"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "by reason only of that fact"; a trustee connected on another ground is outside it

-- (e): "'body corporate' includes a body incorporated outside Singapore, but does not include (i) a corporation sole; or (ii) a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed."
-- src:4523 | (e) “body corporate” includes a body incorporated outside
-- src:4524 | Singapore, but does not include —
-- src:4526 | (i) a corporation sole; or
-- src:4528 | (ii) a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is
-- src:4529 | not regarded as a body corporate under the law by
-- src:4530 | which it is governed.
@ref s 25D(2)(e) (src:4523-4530)
GIVEN `the body is incorporated outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a corporation sole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25D(2)(e) the body is within the words body corporate` MEANS
    IF    `the body is a corporation sole`
       OR `the body is a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'body corporate' ... does not include — (i) a corporation sole; or (ii) a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed"
    ELSE (IF `the body is incorporated outside Singapore`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "'body corporate' includes a body incorporated outside Singapore" does not close the meaning; a body incorporated in Singapore is not named

§ `Section 25D(1): a person connected with a director`

-- The facts about one person, relative to one director of the company. A record: every field is a fact a witness can state.
DECLARE `s 25D(1) person` HAS
    `s 25D(1)(a) the person is a member of the director's family` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(b) the person is a body corporate with which the director is connected within the meaning of subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(c) the person acts in the person's capacity as trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(c)(i) the beneficiaries of the trust include the director or a person who by virtue of paragraph (a) or (b) is connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(c)(ii) the terms of the trust confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or a person mentioned in sub-paragraph (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(c) the trust is for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(d)(i) the person acts in the person's capacity as partner of the director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(d)(ii) the person acts in the person's capacity as partner of a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(e) the person is a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(e)(i) the director is a partner in the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(e)(ii) a partner in the firm is a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(e)(iii) a partner in the firm is a firm in which the director is a partner or in which there is a partner who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 25D(1)(f) the person is himself or herself a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (c) as a whole: trustee, with (i) or (ii), other than a trust for an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme.
GIVEN person IS A `s 25D(1) person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25D(1)(c) the person is within paragraph (c)` MEANS
        person's `s 25D(1)(c) the person acts in the person's capacity as trustee of a trust`
    AND (   person's `s 25D(1)(c)(i) the beneficiaries of the trust include the director or a person who by virtue of paragraph (a) or (b) is connected with the director`
         OR person's `s 25D(1)(c)(ii) the terms of the trust confer a power on the trustees that may be exercised for the benefit of the director or a person mentioned in sub-paragraph (i)`)
    AND (NOT person's `s 25D(1)(c) the trust is for the purposes of an employees' share scheme or a pension scheme`)

-- (d): partner of the director, or of a person connected by (a), (b) or (c).
GIVEN person IS A `s 25D(1) person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25D(1)(d) the person is within paragraph (d)` MEANS
        person's `s 25D(1)(d)(i) the person acts in the person's capacity as partner of the director`
     OR person's `s 25D(1)(d)(ii) the person acts in the person's capacity as partner of a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director`

-- (e): a firm that is a legal person, with (i), (ii) or (iii).
GIVEN person IS A `s 25D(1) person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25D(1)(e) the person is within paragraph (e)` MEANS
        person's `s 25D(1)(e) the person is a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
    AND (   person's `s 25D(1)(e)(i) the director is a partner in the firm`
         OR person's `s 25D(1)(e)(ii) a partner in the firm is a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director`
         OR person's `s 25D(1)(e)(iii) a partner in the firm is a firm in which the director is a partner or in which there is a partner who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the director`)

-- "a reference to a person connected with a director means" (a) to (e), and (f) "does not include a person who is himself or herself a director of the company".
-- A "means" definition is closed: a person within none of (a) to (e) is not connected (JUST FALSE), and (f) is a flat negative (JUST FALSE).
-- src:4432 | 25D.—(1) For the purposes of section 25C, a reference to a person
-- src:4433 | connected with a director means —
-- src:4435 | (a) a member of the director’s family;
-- src:4437 | (b) a body corporate with which the director is connected
-- src:4438 | within the meaning of subsection (2)(b);
-- src:4440 | (c) a person acting in the person’s capacity as trustee of a
-- src:4441 | trust —
-- src:4446 | (i) the beneficiaries of which include the director or a
-- src:4447 | person who by virtue of paragraph (a) or (b) is
-- src:4448 | connected with the director; or
-- src:4450 | (ii) the terms of which confer a power on the trustees that
-- src:4451 | may be exercised for the benefit of the director or any
-- src:4452 | person mentioned in sub‑paragraph (i),
-- src:4454 | (c) other than a trust for the purposes of an employees’ share
-- src:4455 | scheme or on a pension scheme;
-- src:4457 | (d) a person acting in the person’s capacity as partner —
-- src:4459 | (i) of the director; or
-- src:4461 | (ii) of a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c),
-- src:4462 | is connected with that director;
-- src:4464 | (e) a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is
-- src:4465 | governed and in which —
-- src:4467 | (i) the director is a partner;
-- src:4469 | (ii) a partner is a person who, by virtue of paragraph (a),
-- src:4470 | (b) or (c), is connected with the director; or
-- src:4472 | (iii) a partner is a firm in which the director is a partner or
-- src:4473 | in which there is a partner who, by virtue of
-- src:4474 | paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is connected with the
-- src:4475 | director; and
-- src:4477 | (f) a reference to a person connected with a director of a
-- src:4478 | company does not include a person who is himself or
-- src:4479 | herself a director of the company.
@ref s 25D(1) (src:4432-4479)
GIVEN person IS A `s 25D(1) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25D(1) the person is a person connected with the director` MEANS
    IF person's `s 25D(1)(f) the person is himself or herself a director of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(f) a reference to a person connected with a director of a company does not include a person who is himself or herself a director of the company"
    ELSE (IF    person's `s 25D(1)(a) the person is a member of the director's family`
             OR person's `s 25D(1)(b) the person is a body corporate with which the director is connected within the meaning of subsection (2)(b)`
             OR `s 25D(1)(c) the person is within paragraph (c)` person
             OR `s 25D(1)(d) the person is within paragraph (d)` person
             OR `s 25D(1)(e) the person is within paragraph (e)` person
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to a person connected with a director means — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ...; (e) ..." (a "means" definition: a person within none of the paragraphs is not connected)
